==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|o}}

===Etymology===
From *lowna ("day, midday"). Cognates include Karelian {{m|krl|lounat||evening/main meal}}, Veps {{m|vep|louna}}, Votic {{m|vot|lõunaz||south, lunch}}, Estonian {{m|et|lõuna||south, lunch}}, and Udmurt {{m|udm|lun}}. Permic cognates have the meaning "day", whereas Baltic-Finnic cognates denote the direction where the Sun is at midday or the meal eaten at midday.

The compass point meaning was clarified in the 19th century; in earlier text and dialects ''lounas'' may mean either south, southwest or southeast.<ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

